WorldOS Source-Available Commercial EULA v1.0

License type: Custom source-available commercial EULA, not OSI open source.
SPDX-License-Identifier: LicenseRef-WorldOS-Source-Available-Commercial-1.0

Copyright (c) 2026 ElectricSheep

This WorldOS Source-Available Commercial EULA ("Agreement") governs Your use
of WorldOS unless ElectricSheep signs a separate written agreement with You.
This Agreement is inspired by engine-style commercial licensing: You can inspect,
learn from, modify, and build with the source, but commercial rights depend on
the license tier and Royalty Addendum below.

This Agreement is not legal advice. If You plan to ship a commercial Project
using WorldOS, review these terms with counsel and contact ElectricSheep for any
custom commercial agreement or buyout.

1. Prior MIT Grants

Copies of the project that were obtained under the prior MIT license remain
licensed under that prior license for those copies. This Agreement applies to
this version and later versions that include this Agreement unless ElectricSheep
states otherwise in writing.

2. What ElectricSheep Licenses To You

"WorldOS Technology" means WorldOS source code, runtime code, tools, examples,
documentation, project-authored content, and other materials in this repository
unless a file or directory states a different license.

"Runtime Code" means WorldOS code or components needed to run a Project for
users or players, including the playable tabletop/game shell, agentic world
simulation, runtime services, generated-play loop, or a substantially complete
WorldOS-derived playable experience.

"Examples" means sample code, sample worlds, sample campaigns, templates, and
documentation examples that ElectricSheep marks or presents as examples.

"Generated Output" means text, data, designs, exports, world bibles, campaign
notes, maps, static files, images, lore documents, or other materials generated
with or exported from WorldOS.

"Project" means a game, tabletop product, tool, campaign, world, export,
prototype, build, release, service, or other work made with, incorporating, or
derived from WorldOS Technology.

"Distribute" means to sell, license, publish, transfer, host, stream, provide
access to, make available over a network, or otherwise provide a Project or
WorldOS Technology to another person or entity.

"Commercial Use" means use that is intended for, connected to, or results in
commercial advantage, revenue, funding, paid distribution, paid services,
publisher-backed development, monetization, or business operations.

"Non-Commercial Use" means personal, educational, evaluation, research, hobby,
home tabletop, or internal learning use that is not Commercial Use.

"You" means the individual or legal entity using WorldOS.

3. Source-Available Status

WorldOS is source-available software. It is not open source, and this Agreement
is not an OSI-approved license. You may not describe WorldOS as open source
unless ElectricSheep separately releases the relevant materials under an
OSI-approved license.

4. Non-Commercial License

ElectricSheep grants You a worldwide, royalty-free, non-exclusive,
non-transferable, revocable license to use, copy, modify, and run WorldOS
Technology for Non-Commercial Use.

You may share modified source code or patches for Non-Commercial Use if You
preserve this Agreement, preserve copyright and attribution notices, and clearly
mark material changes.

5. Commercial License Tiers

Commercial Use is permitted only under the applicable commercial tier below,
the Royalty Addendum in ROYALTY-ADDENDUM.md, and this Agreement.

5.1 Indie Commercial License

You qualify for the Indie Commercial License only if, when Commercial Use begins
and throughout the Project's commercial life:

- You and Your company have less than USD $1,000,000 in annual gross revenue;
- You and Your company have raised less than USD $1,000,000 in funding;
- the Project is not publisher-backed, publisher-funded, or publisher-directed;
  and
- the company or team has 10 or fewer employees and contractors working on the
  Project.

If You qualify and pay the USD $20 Project fee when Commercial Use begins,
ElectricSheep grants You a worldwide, non-exclusive, non-transferable
commercial license to use, copy, modify, run, reproduce, Distribute, and
otherwise exploit WorldOS Technology in connection with that Project, subject to
this Agreement and the Royalty Addendum.

5.2 Studio Commercial License

The Studio Commercial License applies from day one of Commercial Use if You,
Your company, or the Project has any of the following:

- more than USD $1,000,000 in annual gross revenue;
- more than USD $1,000,000 in funding;
- publisher-backed, publisher-funded, or publisher-directed development; or
- more than 10 employees and contractors working on the Project.

Under the Studio Commercial License, ElectricSheep grants You a worldwide,
non-exclusive, non-transferable commercial license to use, copy, modify, run,
reproduce, Distribute, and otherwise exploit WorldOS Technology in connection
with the Project, subject to this Agreement and the Royalty Addendum unless a
separate written agreement replaces these terms.

If You stop qualifying for the Indie Commercial License, You must move to the
Studio Commercial License or a separate written commercial agreement before
continuing Commercial Use.

6. Distribution Of Projects

You may Distribute a Project that incorporates Runtime Code only as an
integrated part of that Project and only to the extent necessary for users or
players to use the Project. You may not provide WorldOS Technology as a
standalone engine, source-available product, SDK, marketplace, hosted service,
or competing platform.

You may let end users use the incorporated WorldOS Technology solely as part of
Your Project. You may not grant end users the right to extract WorldOS
Technology for their own projects or to use WorldOS Technology independently of
Your Project.

7. Non-Royalty Uses

The following uses do not owe royalties to ElectricSheep by themselves:

- Non-Commercial Use;
- private internal evaluation, research, and learning;
- private home tabletop campaigns that are not monetized;
- Generated Output used privately or internally and not sold, licensed,
  monetized, publisher-backed, or included in a commercial Project;
- screenshots, rendered media, pitch images, or static previews that do not
  themselves generate revenue or provide paid Project access; and
- indirect revenue that is not attributable to Project access, Project features,
  in-Project benefits, or a commercial release shaped by WorldOS.

These exclusions do not remove royalties owed under the Royalty Addendum when
WorldOS is used for a qualifying commercial Project or when Runtime Code ships.

8. Ownership

As between You and ElectricSheep, You own Your original Project, including Your
original game content, tabletop content, campaign content, characters, settings,
art, audio, and Generated Output, except for WorldOS Technology and third-party
materials.

ElectricSheep owns WorldOS Technology, WorldOS trademarks, and all ElectricSheep
intellectual property. No rights are granted by sale, implication, estoppel, or
otherwise except as expressly stated in this Agreement.

9. Third-Party Materials and Separate Licenses

This Agreement does not apply to materials that state a different license,
including but not limited to:

- SRD data and other Creative Commons materials;
- world seeds with their own LICENSE.md files;
- unofficial fan-content seeds and third-party setting material;
- vendored runtime libraries and icon assets;
- trademarks, logos, brand assets, and rights of publicity; and
- private imported content that is not intended for publication.

See THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md, data/srd/ATTRIBUTION.md, and per-world LICENSE.md
files for those terms. Separate third-party terms control if they conflict with
this Agreement for those third-party materials.

10. Restrictions

You may not:

- remove or obscure copyright, license, attribution, or third-party notices;
- use WorldOS for Commercial Use except under the applicable commercial terms
  or a separate written agreement;
- sell, sublicense, host, or provide WorldOS Technology itself as a competing
  engine, platform, hosted service, marketplace, SDK, or source-available
  product;
- use ElectricSheep, WorldOS, ClawDnD, OpenWorlds, or related names, logos, or
  marks in a way that implies endorsement or ownership;
- combine WorldOS Technology with code or content under terms that would require
  WorldOS Technology to be governed by another license;
- commit or redistribute private, imported, user-owned, unpublished, or
  third-party-restricted content from gitignored private paths; or
- use third-party materials in this repository outside their own license terms.

11. Contributions

Outside contributions are accepted only under the WorldOS Contributor License
Agreement in CLA.md unless ElectricSheep agrees otherwise in writing.

12. Custom Agreements

Custom buyouts, capped royalties, enterprise terms, publisher terms, custom
support, and other commercial arrangements are available only by a separate
written agreement signed by ElectricSheep.

If ElectricSheep signs a separate written agreement for a Project, that written
agreement controls for that Project.

13. Notices and Amendments

If ElectricSheep changes this Agreement, You are not required to accept the
amended Agreement for copies of WorldOS Technology You already obtained under
this Agreement. New downloads, updates, services, or repository versions may be
conditioned on accepting the then-current Agreement.

14. No Warranty

WorldOS is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, express or implied,
including but not limited to warranties of merchantability, fitness for a
particular purpose, title, and non-infringement.

15. Limitation of Liability

To the maximum extent permitted by law, ElectricSheep and contributors are not
liable for any claim, damages, lost profits, lost revenue, loss of data,
business interruption, or other liability arising from or related to WorldOS,
whether in contract, tort, or otherwise, even if advised of the possibility of
such damages.

16. Termination

If You violate this Agreement, Your rights under this Agreement terminate
automatically. ElectricSheep may reinstate rights in writing after the violation
is cured. Sections intended to survive termination, including payment
obligations, restrictions, ownership, third-party notices, warranty disclaimers,
and liability limits, survive termination.
